cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GERB, please cite the paper and the archived release below."
title: "GERB: Graduate Economic Reasoning Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark of sixty graduate-level analytical economics problems with verified answers and
  worked reference solutions, fielded in a 2x2 within-task design that crosses a content-preserving
  red herring with an explanation request, to measure whether a red herring, text that looks relevant but is not
  needed to solve the problem, corrupts economic reasoning through distraction. Public design and private content.
type: dataset
